y said Mexican experts were allegedly recruited by a Nigerian national to run a meth laboratory in the southeastern state of Enugu.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Nigeria's upcoming election marred by rising AI disinformation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:229044eb65f29fe020e51c060c2c09d06a6ce00955bf9d10d2d64b446e7d10e6</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:28Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T15:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nigeria-s-upcoming-election-marred-by-rising-ai-disinformation/a-79946897--e1618bd315dd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nigeria-s-upcoming-election-marred-by-rising-ai-disinformation/a-79946897?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As Nigeria inches closer to the 2027 polls, the use of artificial intelligence in the electoral process has prompted questions about integrity and institutional readiness. Can Nigerians trust their democratic processes?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Houthis claim attacks on Saudi refinery, financial district</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:394c30f567a0a0a618bbc6b163694e6f8184cadf6dcf4f682640803c746baa0b</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:28Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T10:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/houthis-claim-attacks-on-saudi-refinery-financial-district/a-80043632--c6099b35575b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/houthis-claim-attacks-on-saudi-refinery-financial-district/a-80043632?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Iran-backed Yemeni Houthis say they carried out fresh retaliatory attacks in Saudi Arabia. A fire was reported at Ras Tanura oil refinery and Riyadh's financial district was attacked for the second time in a week.</summary><category term="News" /></entry></feed>
